<para id="RM000003YYX02SX" category="J" type-id="804JL" name-id="653G0-01" from="200912">
<dtccode/>
<dtcname>USB memory or "iPod" cannot be recognized / cannot be played</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM000003YYX02SX_04" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000IKC00000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E195398J01" width="7.106578999in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000003YYX02SX_02" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___0000IK600000">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>If there are many folders or files in the USB memory, it takes time before playback starts.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When using a USB memory, files that are copy-protected or encrypted cannot be played.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If files on the USB memory are not played in sorted order, perform the following procedure.</ptxt>
</item>
<list2 type="ordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Add numbers to the beginning of the file names.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Move the files into a folder and copy the files to the USB memory folder by folder.</ptxt>
</item>
</list2>
<item>
<ptxt>Depending on the part replaced, setting work may be necessary. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000002RM03SX"/>)</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000003YYX02SX_03" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM000003YYX02SX_03_0007" proc-id="RM0550J___0000IK700000">
<testtitle>Inspect USB Memory or "iPod"</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect the USB memory or "iPod" from stereo jack adapter assembly NO.1.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Check whether playable files exist in the USB memory or "iPod".</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Check that the customer's USB memory or "iPod" is of a supported format and version.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<ptxt>For playable files, supported formats and versions, refer to <xref label="Seep01" href="RM00000014J044X"/>.</ptxt>
</atten4>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.13in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Playable files exist</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>USB memory is of a supported format</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>"iPod" is of a supported version</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>No playable files exist</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>USB memory is not of a supported format</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>"iPod" is not of a supported version</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000003YYX02SX_03_0021" fin="false">A</down>
<right ref="RM000003YYX02SX_03_0002" fin="true">B</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
